# Build context for front_web/Dockerfile.
#
# The tree is large mostly because of things the image never uses: `build/` holds the last
# electron-builder output (a ~500 MB dmg + zip), `node_modules` is reinstalled inside the image,
# and `electron-dist`/`dist-web` are regenerated. Excluding them keeps the context at a few hundred
# MB instead of a few GB.

# Dependencies and build output (regenerated in the image)
node_modules
dist-web
electron-dist
packages/*/dist
packages/*/*.tsbuildinfo
**/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo

# electron-builder output — the desktop feed is published separately, never served by this image
build

# Generated protobuf transport. 5 MB of checked-in TypeScript, and the web bundle *does* import it:
# `src/ts/lib/util/exportReport.ts` and the export-result popup read `Proto/pkg/lib/pb/model/protos/*`,
# which the `Proto` alias in vite.web.config.ts resolves to `front_web/middleware`. Excluding it
# fails `pnpm build` inside the image with `Could not load /app/middleware/...` while the host build
# keeps working off the local checkout.

# Local + reference-only trees
_archive_src
.agents
.qoder
docs

# VCS / editor / OS noise
.git
.gitignore
.husky
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store

# Local env and logs
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.log
logs
